      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Actually, I am not asserting that including all trans women inherently ruins fairness for everyone; rather, I am arguing that a rigid exclusion based solely on gender identity is currently applied arbitrarily and dangerously. The core argument is that we must establish clear, objective biological criteria because relying on self-identified \"gender\" without verified data creates a loophole for some while unfairly ignoring the physiological reality for others in equal sex categories. True fairness isn't just a feeling of being right but ensuring the safety and integrity of competition by using the most accurate biological differentiators available, which for now means a more nuanced approach than the current binary oversight.",
